WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.740
- [Mark] All right, Octavio.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:05.980
Octavio, where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.200
Where are you from?

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.233
- I grew up around the
San Fernando Valley.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.087
- [Mark] And tell me about your family.

00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:12.620
You had both your parents growing up?

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.210
- [Octavio] Yes, I did, yes I did.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.665
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:00:15.665 --> 00:00:17.100
- Interesting.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.660
I was like the black sheep of the family

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.690
and I used to get in
trouble a lot from parents.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.680
They were strict,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.070
they were real strict and
my brothers and sisters,

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.510
they were kind of like goody two-shoes

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.770
and I was opposite.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.980
I was always in trouble around gangs.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.729
I got in a gang at 12 years old.

00:00:35.729 --> 00:00:36.562
- [Mark] 12?
- Yeah.

00:00:36.562 --> 00:00:37.395
- Started one of the gangs.

00:00:37.395 --> 00:00:39.490
We started a clique around my neighborhood

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:42.300
and still today it's up and going.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.440
- [Mark] And you're still active today?

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.287
- Yes, I am, very active.

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.756
- [Mark] Tell me about
your first gang experience.

00:00:49.756 --> 00:00:53.589
- My first gang experience
is just, basically,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.730
just hanging out with my new brothers.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.930
They became my family,
you know what I mean?

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.688
And just growing up with them

00:01:05.688 --> 00:01:06.521
it was like,

00:01:06.521 --> 00:01:07.730
it was different from
growing up with my brothers

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.410
'cause my brothers were, like I said,

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.210
goody two-shoes and they were always

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.140
real snotty, you know what I mean?

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:16.973
Good grades and whatever,

00:01:16.973 --> 00:01:18.760
and I was the opposite.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.566
I mean, I haven't done anything wrong.

00:01:20.566 --> 00:01:21.720
I got good grades, I attended school

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.921
and I did what I had to do,

00:01:22.921 --> 00:01:25.640
but for me, I used to go to school

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:26.590
just to be with my homeboys,

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:29.283
keep my homeboys and the
homegirls and hang around.

00:01:30.736 --> 00:01:31.569
And then we got,

00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:36.047
the first of all was just getting together

00:01:39.024 --> 00:01:40.320
and just hanging out,
you know what I mean?

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.083
Drinking, drugs wasn't even
really a problem back then.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.500
It was smoke a little weed, drink,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:52.283
and then we started using
PCP and other drugs.

00:01:53.282 --> 00:01:56.558
Not really abusing them, but just,

00:01:56.558 --> 00:02:00.360
the weekends go use them and drink, party,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.310
shoot up, hang and do
whatever you got to do,

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:05.360
to survive out there.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.820
We used to hang around a
liquor store in my hood,

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:14.290
the parks, and there'd
be maybe like 50, 60

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:16.160
of us hanging at the park.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.730
Yeah, and then people,

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.060
our enemies would come.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.140
We have, within my neighborhood

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.520
we'd have to drive through,

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.410
it was a cruise spot,

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.880
so there was neighborhoods
from all over coming

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:32.170
to my neighborhood and we'd
get into it with all of them

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.480
'cause it was our hood,

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.045
so we didn't let no one come in.

00:02:35.045 --> 00:02:35.878
You know what I mean?

00:02:35.878 --> 00:02:36.750
They came in, we're on them.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:39.090
And they come up in my hood,

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.430
it was like, they were
getting the bad end of it

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.520
'cause it was our hood.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.520
We knew the escapes and how to get to them

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.510
and how to block 'em in 'cause
it was a drive-through mall

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:52.370
and one car is this and go come this way,

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.620
so you're gonna come
one way in, one way out.

00:02:56.571 --> 00:03:00.337
And we'd get 'em in the mall
and they'd be in trouble.

00:03:00.337 --> 00:03:02.220
And they'd come and tell ya another thing

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.480
and we'd be going back and forth

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.320
and we'd be killing each other.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.280
I think '84 and '85 I
lost about nine homeboys

00:03:08.874 --> 00:03:10.583
and it was a bad year for us.

00:03:13.839 --> 00:03:17.307
Right now I'm 54 years old
and I survived over there,

00:03:18.389 --> 00:03:21.253
but I guess God has another
plan for me in life.

00:03:22.648 --> 00:03:25.020
Right now I strive to be a
productive member of society

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:25.930
and I wanna do good.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:27.510
I'm trying, I'm struggling,

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.450
and it's just hard for me right now.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:30.923
And I've tried programs.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.720
My addiction is what's
keeping me down now.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:36.780
It ain't about...

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.160
I come out of jail or prison, I've been,

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.351
I did 25 years in prison.

00:03:41.351 --> 00:03:43.736
That's just CDC, California
Department of Corrections,

00:03:43.736 --> 00:03:44.569
I already did that.

00:03:45.877 --> 00:03:49.160
And I come out of jail and
I know nothing but prison,

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:53.238
I know nothing but the
life I lived before.

00:03:53.238 --> 00:03:55.690
And for me, for using drugs, it's not...

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.640
It's my downfall, yeah,

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.640
but more my downfall now, my old behavior,

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.830
because once I go be like my old behavior,

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.780
it's like everything falls in place.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.680
You got drugs, women, and
whatever else you got,

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.760
you know what I mean?

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.480
And gang life, surviving the gang life.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.860
Still today, like I said,

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.280
I'm still doing any old shit,

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.796
doing what I'm not supposed to be doing.

00:04:20.796 --> 00:04:21.629
You know what I mean?

00:04:21.629 --> 00:04:22.620
And I'm getting away with it.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.283
Like I said, I wanna be a
productive member of society.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.120
And my time will come.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.973
Right now I'm working on a few things,

00:04:35.485 --> 00:04:37.440
I wanna start gang intervention
for the youngsters,

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.040
I wanna do that for them.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.960
I wanna give back something
that wasn't given to me,

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.530
give something that wasn't given to me.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.580
You know what I mean?

00:04:45.447 --> 00:04:47.670
And for the youngsters to give
themselves a chance in life,

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.660
'cause right when growing up,

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.853
you only know one way and that's the way

00:04:52.853 --> 00:04:54.490
that we can use our environment,

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.240
the people we run with, the people,

00:04:57.117 --> 00:04:59.540
what we see on the street coming

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.310
out our front door.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:02.960
It's like gang life.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.163
So right away, you already
don't have a choice.

00:05:05.163 --> 00:05:06.500
I mean, you do have a choice,

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.910
but you don't make the right choice

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.893
'cause you always go the wrong way.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:18.213
My thing is this, if you're under 18,

00:05:19.214 --> 00:05:21.430
you're not supposed to make
decisions on your own anyways,

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.850
but you do, but you
shouldn't make that decision

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:28.810
to be in a gang first,
you know what I mean?

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.917
Say once you're 18 years
old and graduate high school

00:05:31.917 --> 00:05:33.250
and you decide you wanna go to the gang,

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.143
then that's to go that route.

00:05:36.177 --> 00:05:37.810
But if you graduate from high school,

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.410
you're not gonna go the gang life.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.030
You're gonna do good.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:43.690
'Cause most of the gang members
don't graduate high school.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:45.153
But you end up getting your GED in prison

00:05:45.153 --> 00:05:47.343
because my education was in prison.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.170
I took plumbing, got my GED,

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.250
and then I took an apprentice prep program

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:56.090
at Pasadena City College and I graduated.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.750
And I got a union job, but like I said,

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.260
right now my addiction is,

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:01.610
my addiction bring it down.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:06.430
- [Mark] Is it the drug
that's your biggest problem,

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:08.322
or is it the gang life?

00:06:08.322 --> 00:06:09.270
- It's the drugs right now.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.894
It's drugs, yeah, I'm
struggling right now.

00:06:11.894 --> 00:06:13.743
- [Mark] What's your drug? Heroine?

00:06:14.876 --> 00:06:17.099
- I don't wanna say, but
yeah, pretty much, yeah.

00:06:17.099 --> 00:06:19.152
- [Mark] A lot of the gang
members find heroine too.

00:06:19.152 --> 00:06:20.430
- It's heroine, it's heroine.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.200
- [Mark] Especially in these panic ones.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.183
- I struggle, like I said, I'm struggling.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:26.197
The corps send me to programs

00:06:26.197 --> 00:06:27.680
and I end up fucking them up

00:06:28.779 --> 00:06:32.950
and I want a chance,
eh, I wanna give my...

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.190
It's hard for me right now, man.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.740
I'm really struggling, dude.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:36.790
It's hard, real hard.

00:06:37.775 --> 00:06:39.040
- [Mark] What was the prison time for?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.083
- Prison time for different things.

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:46.050
Just like assaults,

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.133
firearms,

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:52.280
possession for sales, sales of narcotics,

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.380
just things like that.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.880
Car jacking, I car jacked.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:58.360
I got seven years for a
carjack I didn't even do,

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.950
but I'm not gonna snitch on my homeboy

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:02.600
so I took the rap and I got
seven years for it, yeah.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.720
Shit like that, you know, just.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.733
I caught a case in prison, jail.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:13.690
Like I said, I'm struggling man.

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:16.310
I really wanna go the right way,

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:17.630
but it's hard for me,

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:19.063
it's really hard for me right now.

00:07:19.063 --> 00:07:20.050
- [Mark] Do you have kids?
- It's gonna come.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:20.883
Yes, I do.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.550
I have a lovely daughter
that I love very much,

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:27.620
and I can't say I wanna do it for her

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.370
'cause it gotta be done for myself.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.980
I'm at that point that I'm
desperate to get right,

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.200
you know what I mean?

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.460
I'm really am, you know, it's like,

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:38.470
I wanna do the right thing.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.800
I wanna be, like I said,

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:42.180
a productive member of society.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.013
That's what I wanna do.

00:07:43.013 --> 00:07:43.846
You know what I mean?

00:07:43.846 --> 00:07:45.626
- [Mark] Were you in your daughter's life?

00:07:45.626 --> 00:07:46.920
- Nah, I just call her.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.940
I'm not in her life really at all,

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:50.580
just by phone calls and I haven't seen her

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:52.339
in like three years.

00:07:52.339 --> 00:07:53.480
That's a long time.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.130
And I call up my mom.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:58.360
I don't see her either, but
I talk to them on the phone,

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:01.730
but maybe once a month if I'm not in jail.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:04.800
Even in jail, I try to
call them once in awhile.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:08.260
But relationship, I don't
have with them at all

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:09.619
as far as what I want to.

00:08:09.619 --> 00:08:11.287
What I would like to,
I would like to be in

00:08:11.287 --> 00:08:12.940
in their life completely but I'm not.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:16.100
- [Mark] So the fact that
you're siblings walked

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:19.163
a very straight path and
yours was very different,

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.873
what do you think set you on this path?

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:27.520
Was it just the way your brain is wired?

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:28.353
- I don't know.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:31.320
It's not even the drug no more, it's not.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.470
It's not, it's miserable.

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:36.407
I'm miserable right now,
you know what I mean?

00:08:37.981 --> 00:08:40.427
I don't know what it's gonna take,

00:08:40.427 --> 00:08:41.297
I don't know what it's gonna take

00:08:41.297 --> 00:08:42.770
for me to get right.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:45.200
I'm trying, I want it, I
want it, I want it so bad.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.650
It's like, man, I just need the help

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.470
and the program's not helping me.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:52.750
It's like, no one's hitting me-

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:53.583
- [Mark] Have you been through rehabs?

00:08:53.583 --> 00:08:54.416
- In the head with a hammer

00:08:54.416 --> 00:08:55.980
and knock it in so I
could do the right thing.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:58.093
I don't know, I don't
know what I could do.

00:08:58.093 --> 00:08:59.280
- [Mark] Have you tried
rehabs and stuff like that?

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:01.366
- I've tried rehabs, and I get,

00:09:01.366 --> 00:09:03.330
I wanna go, I wanna try rehab again.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:05.009
I do wanna go to rehab.

00:09:05.009 --> 00:09:06.960
It's a start, you know what I mean?

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:08.410
To go in the right direction,

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:13.599
but I came out of jail and recently,

00:09:13.599 --> 00:09:16.099
a month and a half ago and
I wanna go to a program

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:22.060
'cause that way I can come
into society little by little.

00:09:22.301 --> 00:09:24.590
Do the program and then go to outpatient,

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:26.858
you know, stuff like that and sober living

00:09:26.858 --> 00:09:29.170
and just try to do the right thing,

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:31.400
but it's difficult right
now to get into a program

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:35.860
'cause coronavirus has a
lowered down the intake

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:36.790
for the program.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:39.070
- [Mark] What is your biggest regret?

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:40.970
- Right now my biggest regret is, hmm,

00:09:44.287 --> 00:09:48.823
I have a lot of regrets, lot of regrets.

00:09:48.823 --> 00:09:53.543
Man, I mean, my regrets are just,

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:59.501
I guess, joining the gang.

00:09:59.501 --> 00:10:03.180
It really brought me to
this lifestyle I'm in now,

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.480
you know what I mean?

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:05.480
Led me there.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:06.313
- [Mark] What kind of,

00:10:06.313 --> 00:10:07.840
tell me the craziest stories you got

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:08.970
from your gang, gang life?

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:10.660
- Craziest stories in the gang, in prison

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:11.991
or out of prison?

00:10:11.991 --> 00:10:13.430
I've seen a lot of things.

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.730
I got post-traumatic stress disorder

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:16.540
from things I've seen in
prison and on the street.

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:17.845
- [Mark] Oh, is that right?

00:10:17.845 --> 00:10:19.810
- I just about died, dude died in my arms.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.920
- [Mark] So prison is just
as violent as outside?

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.673
- It can be.

00:10:24.673 --> 00:10:27.930
It is, it's like a lot of
things happen in prison

00:10:28.876 --> 00:10:30.290
that you'd be amazed,
you know what I mean?

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:31.840
Like wow, you know what I mean?

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:32.940
People getting stabbed.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.750
I got stabbed in a riot with

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:39.010
against the northern Mexicans.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.670
Which northerners, they
call them Nortenos,

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:42.120
we don't get along with them.

00:10:44.093 --> 00:10:46.120
We got in the yard, we
had a program together.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.424
We started beefing with each other

00:10:48.424 --> 00:10:51.274
and a riot kicks off and people
getting stabbed and hurt.

00:10:52.613 --> 00:10:54.760
We're the same race, we're the same

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:56.650
and it's like, what the hell?

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:59.470
But nowadays it's not like that no more.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.303
Everybody gets along.

00:11:00.303 --> 00:11:02.830
I mean, I get along, we program together

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:04.723
and we have that respect,

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:09.260
that mutual respect that
there's nothing going on

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:11.524
in the yards right now, the prison yards.

00:11:11.524 --> 00:11:14.040
- [Mark] What kind of stuff
were you involved in outside?

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.013
- As far, outside?

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:19.274
Things get ugly, now it's like, you know.

00:11:19.274 --> 00:11:20.598
- [Mark] You can be vague.

00:11:20.598 --> 00:11:21.533
I don't want you thinking-

00:11:21.533 --> 00:11:24.503
- I don't wanna go too
deep 'cause it's like,

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.160
the gang life we live out here is like,

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:32.190
not no more like before.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.510
Before it was a whole different story.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:36.400
I mean, now it's diluted,
it's like watered down

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:39.957
and it's like people are
already over that, you know?

00:11:39.957 --> 00:11:42.310
'Cause we used to be killing each other,

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:43.540
every week we could have a murder.

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:45.570
We'd hear that someone got killed.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.620
Before it was drive-bys
and not it's not even,

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.360
you don't even hear
about drive-bys no more.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.937
And there used to be four in Los Angeles.

00:11:51.937 --> 00:11:53.723
Every weekend someone got shot.

00:11:55.237 --> 00:11:56.110
People are still getting shot,

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.180
but for other reasons besides gangs,

00:11:58.180 --> 00:11:59.680
you know what I mean?

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:02.740
But it's dangerous out here,
it's still dangerous out here

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.370
but it ain't like before,

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.420
you know what I mean?

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.113
People just doing, I don't know,

00:12:09.113 --> 00:12:11.203
I don't wanna elaborate on all that.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:16.354
But gang life is dangerous.

00:12:16.354 --> 00:12:17.187
- [Mark] What would you say to a young man

00:12:17.187 --> 00:12:18.650
who's considering?

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:19.753
- Go the opposite way.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.003
Give yourself a chance.

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:29.940
Gang life's not for us,
especially the Hispanic community.

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:34.103
We need, we need to stop being suppressed

00:12:34.103 --> 00:12:38.323
and move forward, you know what I mean?

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:40.123
Move forward and,

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.903
I know we could do it, eh?

00:12:42.903 --> 00:12:46.433
As a community we could do
it and do the right thing.

00:12:52.116 --> 00:12:53.240
It's gonna take a lot of work,

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:54.540
but I know we could do it.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:58.700
I wanna do to the gang
intervention for the kids,

00:12:58.700 --> 00:12:59.583
when you go to school and talk to the kids

00:12:59.583 --> 00:13:01.363
that it's not the right way.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:05.440
I'd like to get started
but I have to get some kind

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:08.160
of sponsor and some support

00:13:09.437 --> 00:13:10.980
and that will lead me
in the right direction

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.330
just to get it started.

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:13.770
I want to start the gang straight,

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:16.690
I mean, Scared Straight.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:19.900
It was done by LAPD before by Tony Pierce.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.580
He's from (indistinct).

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.240
and he started it with LAPD

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.680
and it went down, but
I wanna start it again

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:30.100
but not with LAPD but maybe Fluid Center.

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:31.150
You know what I mean?

00:13:33.215 --> 00:13:35.610
Get some kind of intervention

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:37.470
so the kids don't come,

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:39.280
the kids don't think that's
the only choice they got

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.940
is to go in the gangs, 'cause they don't.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:43.720
They have other choices they could do

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:44.920
instead of be in a gang.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.870
And like I said, that's
my main downfall is being

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:49.920
in a gang at a young age

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:51.420
and just starting going that route.

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:53.883
It's like, man, I'm 54
years old right now.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:58.700
It's time, you know what I mean?

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:01.300
Just to kick back, give to the grandkids

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:03.276
what I didn't give to me kids.

00:14:03.276 --> 00:14:08.276
My kid, she didn't
deserve the hand she got.

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:12.410
She should've been with
her dad more closely.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.680
She's doing all right, she's over it,

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:16.270
but you know, I still
feel like she could've had

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:17.870
a lot more from me.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.420
And I would like to give
my mom back her son,

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.600
my daughter back her dad,

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.150
and my brothers back their brother.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:26.940
Stuff like that, you know what I mean?

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.580
I really wanna give it.

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:30.100
They don't have me in
their lives right now

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:32.000
and I would like to be in their lives.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:34.740
It's hard.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.350
It's a little journey for me

00:14:37.487 --> 00:14:38.490
and I'll make it happen.

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:40.380
Eventually, I'll make it happen.

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:42.110
And what got me thinking is,

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.960
what's my, what's it called when they?

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:46.848
Eulogy, eulogy, what's it called?

00:14:46.848 --> 00:14:47.681
- [Mark] Eulogy.

00:14:47.681 --> 00:14:48.730
- Yeah, what's it gonna
look like for my kids,

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:51.660
coming from my daughter,
what's it gonna be?

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:54.310
Oh, Dad died of getting shot.

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:56.100
Or Dad died of a heroine overdose.

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.630
You know what I mean?

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:58.530
What's it gonna say about me?

00:14:58.530 --> 00:14:59.620
What can she say about me?

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:00.690
What does she know about me?

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:01.670
Does she really know me?

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:03.033
No, she don't know me.

00:15:04.016 --> 00:15:05.266
And I want to get to know her

00:15:05.266 --> 00:15:07.270
and I want her to know the real me

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.933
'cause I am a good person, I just,

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:15.400
I'm surprised by all
the bad things in life

00:15:16.382 --> 00:15:18.155
and I wanna change.

00:15:18.155 --> 00:15:19.578
I wanna change, it's what I want.

00:15:19.578 --> 00:15:20.591
That's all I got.

00:15:20.591 --> 00:15:21.582
- [Mark] All right, Octavio,

00:15:21.582 --> 00:15:22.684
thank you so much for sharing your story.

00:15:22.684 --> 00:15:23.517
- Yeah, thank you.

00:15:23.517 --> 00:15:25.767
- [Cameraman] Thanks, man.

